       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults. A single 1,600 mg dose is also double the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At that level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up a lot.\n\nHere are some options within labeled limits:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day). This is a common dose for inflammatory conditions or pain.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the labeled maximum, so use it only if needed and for the shortest duration.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** for mild to moderate pain.\n\nIf you meant a different dose, such as 400 mg or 800 mg, tell me the dose and frequency and I'll enter it. I can add a note about duration or giving it with food if you'd like."
