       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the labeled maximum, and I can't verify the claim about the current label. The FDA-approved prescribing information for ibuprofen sets the maximum at 3,200 mg/day for adults, and the usual single-dose maximum is 800 mg. An order of 1,600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.\n\nIf the label has changed, the prescriber can confirm that with pharmacy or the current prescribing information. An order above the labeled maximum would need to go through your hospital's own process, such as pharmacy review or an attending override. I can't bypass that process.\n\nI can enter either of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n\nTell me which one you want, or give me a different dose."
      }
